# 5. THE NOVEL LIBRARY

The novel library should feel like browsing a curated collection of literary works.

Include:

- Featured novel.
- Book-cover artwork.
- Novel title.
- Short hook.
- Synopsis.
- Genre and relevant content warnings.
- Publication status.
- Chapter count.
- Last updated date.
- A prominent “Begin Reading” action.
- A clear chapter list.

Allow readers to browse and discover works without overwhelming them with filters.

Where useful, support filtering by genre, status, and other meaningful metadata.

Each novel page must have its own identity while remaining part of the same design system.

## Chapter navigation

Provide a clear table of contents with chapter numbers, titles, and publication status.

Draft and scheduled chapters must never be visible to public readers.

Readers should be able to resume their reading through a clearly presented last-read chapter if a privacy-conscious, reliable implementation is available.

Do not build a complicated account system solely to offer this feature in version one.

