# 14. ACCEPTANCE TESTS — DEFINITION OF DONE

The project is not complete simply because the homepage looks beautiful.

Verify the following:

1. A visitor can open the website on a phone and desktop.
2. Visitors can browse novels, short stories, poetry, and journal entries.
3. A novel has an accessible chapter list.
4. Readers can move between published chapters.
5. Chapter typography is comfortable for extended reading.
6. An administrator can log in securely.
7. An administrator can create, edit, draft, publish, and unpublish content without changing code.
8. A newly published chapter appears publicly without a code deployment.
9. A reader can post a chapter-specific comment.
10. The comment remains after refreshing the page.
11. A reader can reply and react to comments.
12. Spoiler handling and reporting work.
13. The author's verified account displays the Author badge.
14. Unauthorized users cannot perform administrative actions.
15. Unpublished content is not publicly accessible.
16. The administrator can moderate comments and reports.
17. Database permissions prevent unauthorized access.
18. Source code and project configuration are accessible to me.
19. The backup process is documented and restoration is feasible.
20. Essential pages have working metadata and sensible error states.

If a test fails, report it clearly and fix it where possible.

