# FINAL CREATIVE DIRECTIVE

Moonfall Fiction should not look like a website that happens to contain dark stories.

**It should feel like the world those stories came from.**

The first screen should make visitors curious. The library should invite exploration. The reading experience should make them forget the interface exists. The chapter discussions should make them feel that other people have been haunted by the same words.

Make the website visually arresting without becoming exhausting. Make it immersive without becoming confusing. Make it elegant without becoming sterile. Make it dark without sacrificing readability.

Build something readers will remember even after they close the tab.

The standard is not “a nice dark website.”

The standard is **a distinctive literary home that earns its place in a reader's bookmarks.**